1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,040
There's a hole in your vision. Right

2
00:00:02,060 --> 00:00:02,850
now.

3
00:00:03,065 --> 00:00:05,175
Want to find it? Close your left eye.

4
00:00:05,195 --> 00:00:06,605
Stare at the cross.

5
00:00:07,005 --> 00:00:09,455
Now slowly bring your phone closer...

6
00:00:09,772 --> 00:00:11,812
until the dot disappears.

7
00:00:13,771 --> 00:00:15,771
That's your blind spot: where your

8
00:00:15,791 --> 00:00:17,971
optic nerve leaves the eye, nothing

9
00:00:17,991 --> 00:00:19,231
detects light.

10
00:00:19,628 --> 00:00:21,688
You never notice, because your brain

11
00:00:21,708 --> 00:00:22,848
paints over it.

12
00:00:23,489 --> 00:00:25,479
And that's not the only edit.

13
00:00:25,796 --> 00:00:27,546
You blink about fifteen times a

14
00:00:27,566 --> 00:00:30,056
minute, and never see the darkness.

15
00:00:30,452 --> 00:00:32,512
Your eyes jump about three times a

16
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:35,322
second. Even now, reading this.

17
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,890
Each jump smears the image, so your

18
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:39,620
brain cuts the blur...

19
00:00:39,781 --> 00:00:41,781
then covers the gap by stretching the

20
00:00:41,801 --> 00:00:43,791
next image back in time.

21
00:00:44,587 --> 00:00:46,057
That's why, when you glance at a

22
00:00:46,077 --> 00:00:48,207
clock, the second hand seems to

23
00:00:48,227 --> 00:00:49,187
freeze.

24
00:00:49,668 --> 00:00:51,868
It didn't. Your brain stretched it.

25
00:00:52,903 --> 00:00:54,803
You're not seeing the world live.

26
00:00:54,823 --> 00:00:56,353
You're seeing an edit.

27
00:00:56,914 --> 00:00:58,804
One so good, you never noticed the

28
00:00:58,824 --> 00:00:59,644
hole...
